Certainly! The HELP and NOOP commands can be added to the sequence of client requests in a way that maintains the logical flow of the FTP session. The HELP command can be used to request help on available commands, and the NOOP command can be used to keep the connection alive.

Here’s a modified sequence of the client requests with HELP and NOOP added:

```
USER ubuntu
PASS ubuntu
SYST
HELP
PWD
PORT 127,0,0,1,132,209
NOOP
LIST
MKD test
QUIT
```

In this sequence:
- The HELP command is placed after the SYST command to inquire about available commands right after logging in.
- The NOOP command is placed after the PORT command to keep the connection active before proceeding with the LIST command. 

Feel free to adjust the placement of HELP and NOOP as needed based on your specific requirements!

